From 84a81a2c9171ca1642e793f475fb52d64cc21dd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Beany <24502088+beanyforever@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:38:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Writers outside WriteTree and saveAttributeView raise what
 they wrote

Patch 0005 gives each page and database a version that WriteTree,
WriteTreeIfUnchanged, fixTreeJSONData's write-back and saveAttributeView
raise, so a cache serves no copy older than their writes. Many other
writers put pages and databases on disk without them: the file API
(putFile, copies, renames, removes), the archive API's unzip, the MCP
file tool, imports, notebook mount and removal, moves across notebooks,
snapshot restores, sync and checkout, the user-guide mount and WebDAV.
After those, the caches kept serving the copy from before, and the next
edit could save it over the file.

- cache.RaisePages and cache.RaiseAVs raise a page or database without
  dropping anything, under the version map's own leaf lock, and
  cache.RaiseAll raises an epoch below which nothing noted is served.
  A database no reader has noted is skipped.
- filesys.RaiseForDataPath raises what a path under data/ names: a .sy
  its page, storage/av/<id>.json its database, a folder everything it
  holds after a walk, and data/ itself everything. BeginDataPathWrite
  brackets a remove, raising what the paths held before and after, and
  at a folder's end raises again whatever was raised since it began, so
  a page written into the folder meanwhile is caught.
  RaiseForDataCopy raises what a copy brought.
- About 60 call sites raise after their write, or bracket it, whether
  or not it succeeded. Moves have no code of their own: their renames
  raise both paths. Sync, checkout and asset recovery raise everything
  on each file dejavu writes or removes, since its events name no
  path, and raise the merge's removed files after; a failed sync or
  checkout, a data.zip import and the user-guide mount raise
  everything.

Rolling a page back to a snapshot it already matched, while the page
was cached, removed its file and then had WriteTree skip the write as
unchanged, leaving no file; the raise at the remove makes WriteTree
write it.

Left open: with on-demand asset downloads, a page a sync removes stays
served until the sync returns, since dejavu removes it with no event
(its test skips that mode); a write that began before a folder remove
and ends after it can still cache the removed page, which needs writers
to take turns; and the CLI writes in its own process.

The patch carries 30 Go tests, each through what SiYuan serves. Of the
ones written before the fix, a writer per kind of bypass, Doc2Heading's
source page, a data.zip import, a sync download and a full checkout
fail without it on v3.8.7 with patches 0001 to 0005, and so does the
snapshot rollback. The rest check a sync read while it uploads, a
folder remove racing a write, by a single writer, a bulk writer and in
a folder larger than the version map, a copy through a link, and the
raises themselves.
